content:
hana: Product asked for a concise changelog note + tiny migration snippet for the new latency-first routing opt-in. Release target 2026-04-27; docs PR due 2026-04-22.

oliver: Ill take the PR. What should the known-issue callout be?

susan: Eng details: new boolean flag routing.prefer_latency (default false). If true, router favors latency-optimized variants and falls back to cost-optimized ones when latency targets can't be met. Known quirk: when a fallback happens during streaming, a short partial chunk can be emitted before the fallback completes.

oliver: Draft changelog line: "Latency-first routing (opt-in): enable routing.prefer_latency to prefer low-latency model variants. Existing integrations unchanged."

oliver: JS snippet to include:
```js
// JS SDK v2
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const out = await client.generate({
  model: 'rwk-1',
  prompt: 'Summarize the changelog',
  routing: { prefer_latency: true }
});
console.log(out.text);
```

oliver: Python snippet will be added too. Also adding migration anchor /docs/migrate/latency-first-routing and a short cache note: enabling this may route across model families and lower prefix/KV cache hit rate temporarily.

deploy-bot: branch created: refs/heads/docs/latency-first-apr27 by oliver (CI queued).

susan: tech signoff: ok. Add rollout note: gradual 72-hour rollout with automatic rollback on error thresholds.

hana: thanks — merge after staging preview. I'll notify support and CS once merged.
